# interplay_lifetime_view_outlives_base: A view holds its base's Metal texture, not its reference. The base is filled red and deleted (37); the next exec makes the base again from its guest page (the guest's texels), while the live view still reads red. A green fill of the new base does not reach the view; the view deleted and made again is a view of the new base, and reads green. A texture over a shared buffer (type 8, commandType 9) whose buffer is deleted keeps the old buffer: its fill still lands in the buffer's guest page in every setup.
